<title>POLAND: NBP OFFERS TO DRAIN PLN 600 MLN FOR 14 DAYS.</title>
<headline>NBP OFFERS TO DRAIN PLN 600 MLN FOR 14 DAYS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland offered to drain 600 million zlotys, in nominal terms, off the market for 14 days through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction, the bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank also offered 400 million zlotys of its</p>
<p>273-day NBP-bills.</p>
<p>    Deadline hour		 - 12:00</p>
<p>    Date of settlement	  - November 8, 1996</p>
<p>    Repurchase		    - November 22 (revrepo)</p>
<p>    Discount rate (pct)	 - 20.00 (revrepo)</p>
<p>Maturity of bills offered - Dec 6, 1996 (revrepo)</p>
<p>					  Aug 8, 1997 (NBP-bills)</p>
<p>	 -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
